# TS core + UI (standing rule)

```text
Backend / mocks (@matchwear/core-api)
    ▲
@matchwear/core-*     ← domain TypeScript, NO React, NO CSS
    ▲
apps/* + @matchwear/ui-web   ← React wiring / visuals only
```

## Always

- New domain logic → `@matchwear/core-*` in **TypeScript** (`.ts`), never JSX/CSS/React
- Shells (`apps/buyer-web`, future Expo) inject ports and render; keep pages thin
- Ask first: *домен или пиксели?* Domain → core even if only one shell exists today
- Controllers / helpers: `createXController`, pure fns — reusable by web / TG / RN

## Mocks live in core-api

- Mock fixtures + in-memory store stay in `@matchwear/core-api` (e.g. `sharedProductStore`)
- Do **not** move mocks into `apps/*` or invent parallel fake data in pages
- When real API lands: swap/implement ports in `core-api` — shells keep the same `core-*` + UI contracts
- Prefer mocks calling domain helpers (`itemDisplayPrice`, etc.) instead of reimplementing formulas

## Don't

- Put filters, totals, stock, status rules, gesture thresholds in `*Page.jsx`
- Import React into `packages/js/core-*`
- Put domain controllers in `@matchwear/ui-web`
- Add ad-hoc mock arrays next to screens when `core-api` already has the port

See `docs/FRONTEND_ARCHITECTURE.md`.

**Docs:** new/changed `@matchwear/core-*` public API → update that package `README.md` (and architecture table if a new package) in the same change (rule: `.cursor/rules/docs-with-code.mdc`).
